WEBVTT

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:17.040
Mom!

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.540
Mom, it's about to start.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.380
As the battle of the champions
is about to begin,

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:28.170
the venue is filled with that
intense excitement we felt

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:28.170
Hurry, hurry!

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:31.050
at Megalonia once more.

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:34.680
The crowd goes wild as both
fighters enter the ring.

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:37.270
Isn't that...?

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:42.900
As Joe had announced before the match,
he is definitely wearing a Gear.

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.860
Yes. I'm sure he'll show us what he
can do with this new fighting style

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:48.490
that's a huge contrast
to his "Gearless" days.

00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:51.030
That's Chief's Gear.

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:53.280
He's actually using it.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:54.870
In the west corner...

00:00:54.870 --> 00:01:00.540
...the first Megalonia champion
and representing Team Nowhere...

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:06.710
The legend is back in the ring!
The Real Boxer, Joe!

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:16.140
You better not lose, Joe!

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.180
And in the east corner...

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:22.480
Ranked number 1 in the IMA
Ranking and our current champion...

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:25.150
Representing Sons of ROSCO...

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:31.990
The Public Hero, Mac Rosario!

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.240
You can do it, Daddy!

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:46.920
Go out there and win, Partner.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:48.250
We're with you.

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:53.550
This venue has been home to some
notable fights ever since Megalonia,

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:58.390
and another historical
fight is about to begin.

00:01:58.390 --> 00:02:01.600
I just want to enjoy the match...

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:04.140
...and you're trying to
get in the way of that.

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:10.820
Am I the one who changed...

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:12.900
...or is it you?

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:17.990
We both turned a blind eye
to inconvenient truths,

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:22.000
not realizing it'd end up in
retaliation from ourselves.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.500
Are you calling that a mistake?

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:26.170
I am ashamed at the fact that

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:30.800
I thought that I was a good judge of
character and was gravely mistaken.

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:37.430
Both fighters head to the middle of the
ring as the match is about to begin.

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:42.680
It's strange, Maya.
I feel so calm right now.

00:02:48.610 --> 00:02:54.240
When you lose your way, the hummingbird
will lead you back home.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:58.990
This Gear was the prized possession
of a man who lived out his dreams.

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:02.750
He must've crossed the sea, too.

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:03.950
Yeah.

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:42.860
MEGALOBOX 2

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:00.320
Joe is showing off his Gear technique.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:03.990
By shifting his body just slightly,
he's able to split up the impact,

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:07.750
and keep the damage
to his body to a minimal.

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:11.080
We're already seeing a dizzying display
of offense vs defense in the first round.

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:15.090
Both fighters are excellent outboxers.

00:05:18.340 --> 00:05:21.430
Not to mention, Mac has his Mac Time,

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:25.260
which allows him to turn
the tables on any match.

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:32.190
Uh-oh! Looks like Mac's already bleeding!

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:37.480
Looks like the same place he was
cut during the match with Liu.

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:39.150
Mac, calm down.

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:41.450
Don't stop! He's gonna get around you!

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:52.000
That is Mac's undisclosed
data before it was falsified.

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:57.920
Sakuma had been telling her to delete any
data showing any problems with BES

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:00.880
but she ignored those orders
and sent that to me.

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:06.640
So BES puts a heavy burden on
the brain, which causes side effects.

00:06:07.850 --> 00:06:10.970
You knew that and didn't
say anything earlier.

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:12.310
Yes.

00:06:12.310 --> 00:06:16.400
She knew what she was doing was wrong.

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:20.190
But she still had the courage
to leak this information.

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:29.160
So she resorted to lying because

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:32.580
she couldn't bear with the
sins she had committed.

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:37.380
Actually, she might not
even know she's lying.

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:39.880
Are you implying that you
had nothing to do with this?

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:41.550
Of course not.

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:44.260
Rather than coming to a
conclusion from the data,

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:47.640
you falsify the data to
meet your conclusion.

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:50.390
Brilliant scientists become overconfident

00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:53.310
and sometimes don't realize
they're doing something wrong.

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:57.810
You must be talking about yourself.

00:06:57.810 --> 00:06:59.690
Pardon?

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:05.320
You were in such a hurry to complete BES,
you falsified another person's future.

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:09.530
What are you talking about?

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:17.250
Mac's being super careful.
He's definitely keeping his distance.

00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:19.630
I wonder if he's worried about a counter.

00:07:19.630 --> 00:07:21.130
Joe.

00:07:21.130 --> 00:07:24.260
Can you get closer this next round?

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:26.970
Yeah. It's not as deep as I thought.

00:07:26.970 --> 00:07:29.600
Once he lowers his head, throw in a hook.

00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:32.140
His vision down below will be
limited due to the bleeding.

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:33.220
Got it.

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:34.980
Are you dizzy or nauseous at all?

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:36.350
I'm good.

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:38.690
Let us know the second
you feel any of that.

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:39.610
Yeah.

00:07:39.610 --> 00:07:42.780
The cut's not deep, but try
not to get hit anymore.

00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:44.570
He's going to aim for that cut.

00:07:44.570 --> 00:07:45.690
I know.

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:47.360
Be careful.

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:50.780
Or your precious time with Joe
will be over before you know it.

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:57.960
Ms. Yoshimura,

00:07:57.960 --> 00:08:02.090
Mac and Maya will be here shortly.
What would you like to do?

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:07.010
I'd like to sit in, if that's all right.

00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:08.380
All right.

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:22.310
I'm so sorry.

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:28.280
I came here so the truth could be known.

00:08:28.280 --> 00:08:33.030
I might be asking for too
much to rely on you now,

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:37.370
but I'm done hurting my family.

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:42.170
Will you help me out so
we can move forward?

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:47.510
Ms. Yoshimura.

00:08:47.510 --> 00:08:50.760
Ms. Asamoto told me about you.

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:54.300
With that in mind, I have a request.

00:08:55.850 --> 00:09:00.020
This is only something you can do since
you've been observing me this whole time.

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:05.690
All of your numbers are normal.

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:08.440
Once it looks like Mac Time
is about to happen,

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:10.780
I will do everything I
can to stop the match!

00:09:16.290 --> 00:09:22.750
Mac and Maya told me everything
about how they got to know you.

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:28.840
So... you're telling me
to pay for my sins?

00:09:28.840 --> 00:09:33.470
There is no atoning or
paying for your sins here.

00:09:33.470 --> 00:09:35.930
You will just have to take responsibility
for what you've done.

00:09:38.810 --> 00:09:40.560
Even then...

00:09:42.270 --> 00:09:45.150
...you've got no right to criticize me!

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:48.690
I mean, you're just as guilty as I am!

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:57.160
What a rollercoaster ride!

00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:59.330
Such an excellent display
of offense and defense!

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:03.920
Mac's bleeding once again.

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:06.630
His cut from earlier must've
opened up again.

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:11.130
Does he have Mac cornered?

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:39.950
One.

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:46.330
The first one down in this match is Joe!

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:44.000
Two.

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:47.840
Three.

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:47.840
Joe!

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:55.180
Four.

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:55.180
Joe!

00:10:57.640 --> 00:10:59.300
Six.

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:01.180
Joe!

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:02.770
Seven.

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:04.730
Over here, Joe! Listen for my voice!

00:11:04.730 --> 00:11:06.230
Eight.

00:11:04.730 --> 00:11:08.610
Over here! Over here!
Concentrate on my voice!

00:11:08.610 --> 00:11:09.940
Nine.

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:21.160
You're going to expose the truth?

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:24.710
You know that you won't be
let off the hook if you do.

00:11:24.710 --> 00:11:27.120
Indeed. And I am prepared for that.

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:33.550
I am in the same position as you. All I
can do is take responsibility for this.

00:11:37.510 --> 00:11:40.720
"People cannot move forward without hope."

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:45.350
You and I both believed that!
We truly did!

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:48.190
And now, you have this
pathetic sense of justice

00:11:48.190 --> 00:11:49.730
and you're trying to dispose of BES!

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:51.650
Now that is abandoning
your responsibility!

00:11:51.650 --> 00:11:52.570
Am I wrong?

00:11:52.570 --> 00:11:56.530
The hope that I believe
in is for humanity.

00:11:56.530 --> 00:12:00.780
You have no right to speak of this
when you've toyed with another's life.

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:05.750
But BES is innocent in all of this.

00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:09.290
Are you trying to strike a deal?

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:11.630
If you let go of BES's license,

00:12:11.630 --> 00:12:16.260
I won't make all of the atrocious
things you did to Mac public.

00:12:16.260 --> 00:12:19.380
This was also Mac's request.

00:12:20.640 --> 00:12:24.260
I'm going to fight Joe my own way.

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:31.900
You're quite the woman.

00:12:31.900 --> 00:12:34.940
I am just another person, not some woman.

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:48.910
Mac!

00:12:48.910 --> 00:12:50.290
Mac goes down!

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:51.670
One.

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:55.670
Mac's numbers are reaching
a dangerous level.

00:12:52.380 --> 00:12:54.500
Two.

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:55.670
Three.

00:12:56.550 --> 00:12:58.550
Four.

00:12:58.550 --> 00:13:00.220
Five.

00:13:00.220 --> 00:13:00.590
Five.

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:02.340
Six.

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:06.770
It's always been my dream...

00:13:06.770 --> 00:13:10.190
I just want to fight
with Joe in that ring.

00:13:10.190 --> 00:13:13.400
That is my final wish.

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:17.190
I never want to lose my family again.

00:13:17.190 --> 00:13:19.190
As long as I can just remember that,

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:21.410
I should be able to stay the real me.

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:35.630
Seven.

00:13:35.630 --> 00:13:38.760
Mac's back on his feet!

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:41.470
Now both fighters have
been knocked down once.

00:13:41.470 --> 00:13:44.760
You can't even look away for a second.

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:46.470
It's strange.

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:49.560
Mac, you, and Yuri

00:13:49.560 --> 00:13:51.940
are all connected with him.

00:13:54.860 --> 00:13:55.770
Boss...

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:59.320
Let's not talk about you getting
back in that ring right now.

00:13:59.320 --> 00:14:00.740
With a match like this,

00:14:00.740 --> 00:14:04.200
even an old man like me would
want to get back into that ring.

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:10.450
That's the kind of match I want to have.

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:12.790
And to make that come true,

00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:16.000
I want to believe in myself one more time.

00:14:18.630 --> 00:14:20.880
Joe! Your guard's down!

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:40.530
Mac had been holding back,
but now he's turning that around!

00:14:40.530 --> 00:14:43.650
Both his speed and precision just shot up.

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:46.620
Did he enter Mac Time?

00:14:46.620 --> 00:14:48.700
No.

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:51.410
But I can't explain it.

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:53.660
His numbers are at a normal level

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:57.000
but he's reaching a
Mac-Time level performance.

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:59.250
Then it's simple.

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:01.800
This is just his actual talent then.

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:08.140
This is my last match.

00:15:08.140 --> 00:15:08.840
Mac!

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:10.430
Daddy!

00:15:10.430 --> 00:15:13.390
I'm going to fight Joe as my true self.

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:04.110
He's going in to get hit.

00:16:04.110 --> 00:16:05.320
Yeah.

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:13.540
You really...

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:16.000
...haven't changed one bit.

00:16:22.170 --> 00:16:23.500
Sachio!

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:28.760
You just want to keep going,
don't you, Joe?

00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:48.900
Joe's second has thrown in the towel!

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:55.160
The winner of this battle of
the century is Mac Rosario!

00:16:56.160 --> 00:17:01.790
Due to Joe's withdrawal,
the champion has won this match!

00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:01.790
That was amazing... They're both amazing.

00:17:05.630 --> 00:17:11.970
It felt like Pops was next to me
and said, "You get to decide."

00:17:15.640 --> 00:17:17.470
He is.

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:18.680
Daddy!

00:17:21.020 --> 00:17:23.110
I'm back.

00:17:23.110 --> 00:17:24.770
Welcome back.

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:25.940
Welcome back, Daddy.

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:26.860
Thanks.

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:28.980
Team Nowhere

00:17:29.570 --> 00:17:31.360
That was a long journey.

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:32.570
Yeah.

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:58.770
Because of our partnership, I believe
that Shirato is also highly responsible

00:17:58.770 --> 00:18:03.100
in this scandal involving
the falsified data.

00:18:03.100 --> 00:18:06.520
We, of course, deserve to be penalized.

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:10.610
But before that, there is something
we must take care of immediately.

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:16.870
We need to fix the problems with BES,
and in order to serve society once more,

00:18:16.870 --> 00:18:21.370
we are opening up the license to
brain chip and Gear technology

00:18:21.370 --> 00:18:24.210
to researchers all around the world
for medical purposes only.

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:28.880
BES has infinite possibilities.

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:34.050
I am sure all of you were moved
from Mac's fight the other day.

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:38.430
The miracle he has caused
is an undeniable truth.

00:18:38.430 --> 00:18:42.680
People cannot move forward without hope.

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:45.940
BES has showed us this light of hope.

00:18:45.940 --> 00:18:49.610
Even if the possibility is small...

00:18:49.610 --> 00:18:55.450
Please never let the light that will lead
our society to a better future go out.

00:18:55.450 --> 00:18:59.580
That is our duty, being alive in this age,

00:18:59.580 --> 00:19:01.410
and we need to see it through.

00:19:03.780 --> 00:19:08.750
"A Huge Flaw in the BES Brain Chip!
ROSCO CEO Sakuma Arrested
Accused of Falsifying Data to Conceal
Evidence and Aggravated Breach of Trust"

00:19:07.250 --> 00:19:08.750
Thank you for everything.

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:12.670
I have nothing but
respect for your decision.

00:19:12.670 --> 00:19:15.930
I am grateful you accepted this offer

00:19:15.930 --> 00:19:19.220
despite knowing how hard
it's going to be for all of you.

00:19:24.690 --> 00:19:27.730
Oh, yes. The next time we're
able to get some time off,

00:19:27.730 --> 00:19:30.070
will you go sneaker shopping with me?

00:19:30.070 --> 00:19:34.070
Yes. You're finally being
freed from those heels.

00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:38.620
I'll see you later, President Asamoto.

00:19:38.620 --> 00:19:40.410
Yes.

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:44.120
"Team Nowhere"

00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:42.120
Good luck, Sachio.

00:19:42.120 --> 00:19:44.040
Never thought you had it in you.

00:19:44.040 --> 00:19:46.330
Why do you always say stuff like that?

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:50.790
"Congratulations on
your new job, Sachio!!"

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:50.710
But it's awesome that you're going
to leave for a while to train.

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:54.470
You better not immediately
come crying back here.

00:19:54.470 --> 00:19:59.680
Yeah, yeah. I can't let Mr. Abuhachi down.

00:19:59.680 --> 00:20:01.560
Here's a parting gift.

00:20:01.560 --> 00:20:05.850
Though you might not need it since
you'll have the latest equipment.

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:07.440
I'll take good care of it.

00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:11.150
Once you become a top-notch mechanic,
I'll write an article about you.

00:20:11.150 --> 00:20:12.980
Maybe if you're still a reporter then.

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:15.320
Look who's talking.

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:15.990
Are you sure about this, Joe?
Letting Sachio go like this.

00:20:15.990 --> 00:20:20.410
Yeah, we might all get separated again.

00:20:20.410 --> 00:20:24.700
Even if that happens, this place
will always be your home.

00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:28.710
You guys can come back here
whenever you feel like it. Right?

00:20:28.710 --> 00:20:30.170
You're going, too, aren't you, Joe?

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:33.210
With Sachio.

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:37.130
Just part of the way.
I'm going to go visit Chief's grave.

00:20:38.680 --> 00:20:40.300
Then I'll be back.

00:20:40.300 --> 00:20:41.890
What?

00:20:41.890 --> 00:20:44.430
It's not like I was worried or anything.

00:20:49.850 --> 00:20:52.190
--Sachio!
--You guys been good?

00:20:52.190 --> 00:20:54.070
It's been a while.

00:20:54.070 --> 00:20:55.440
Welcome back, everyone.

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:57.570
Look at how big you got!

00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:04.120
Sorry for causing you so much trouble.

00:21:04.120 --> 00:21:08.250
Until we got here, they kept saying how
they wanted to stay at our facilities,

00:21:08.250 --> 00:21:11.290
but this is truly their home.

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:13.790
Yeah.

00:21:27.560 --> 00:21:31.690
Welcome to Casa.
We're glad to have you all here.

00:21:31.690 --> 00:21:36.400
Wait right there.
I'm going to make some space.

00:21:36.400 --> 00:21:37.610
Mio?

00:21:47.870 --> 00:21:49.120
What's that?

00:21:49.120 --> 00:21:53.460
This is called <i>braai</i>. It's barbecue
from my home country.

00:21:53.460 --> 00:21:54.670
<i>Braai</i>?

00:21:54.670 --> 00:21:56.630
We all gather around the
fire and enjoy it together.

00:21:56.630 --> 00:21:58.550
That's <i>braai</i>.

00:21:58.550 --> 00:21:59.760
Braai!

00:21:59.760 --> 00:22:01.130
What's that?

00:22:11.350 --> 00:22:15.480
When the electronic signal from the
brain chip spreads to each section,

00:22:15.480 --> 00:22:18.820
the subject's memory code
plays a very important part.

00:22:18.900 --> 00:22:20.650
"Special Lecture The History and Principles
of Brain Chip Development Tomoka Yoshimura"

00:22:20.650 --> 00:22:23.440
Team Nowhere

00:22:22.820 --> 00:22:23.360
Here.

